development.question_text:
Find the points of intersection of the circle $x^{2}+y^{2}=25$ and the line $y=x-1$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.4]
\draw[->] (-6.5,0)--(6.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-6.5)--(0,6.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \n in {5,-5} {\draw (\n,-0.15)--(\n,0.15); \draw (-0.15,\n)--(0.15,\n);}
\draw[thick,blue] (0,0) circle (5);
\draw[thick,red,<->] (-5.5,-6.5)--(6,5);
\node[blue] at (-2.6,5.7) {$x^{2}+y^{2}=25$};
\node[red] at (5.9,3.6) {$y=x-1$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.solution_text:
$y=x-1 \quad (1)$
$x^{2}+y^{2}=25 \quad (2)$
1. **Equate the two equations.**
Substitute $(1)$ into $(2)$: $x^{2}+(x-1)^{2}=25$
2. **Rearrange to a quadratic $ax^{2}+bx+c=0$.**
$x^{2}+x^{2}-2x+1=25$
$2x^{2}-2x-24=0$
$x^{2}-x-12=0$
3. **Solve for the $x$-coordinate(s).**
$(x-4)(x+3)=0$
$x=4 \text{ or } x=-3$
4. **Substitute back to find each $y$-coordinate.**
When $x=4$: $y=4-1=3$
When $x=-3$: $y=-3-1=-4$
The points of intersection are $(4,3)$ and $(-3,-4)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.4]
\draw[->] (-6.5,0)--(6.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-6.5)--(0,6.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue] (0,0) circle (5);
\draw[thick,red,<->] (-5.5,-6.5)--(6,5);
\fill (4,3) circle (0.22);
\fill (-3,-4) circle (0.22);
\node[above right] at (4,3) {$(4,3)$};
\node[below left] at (-3,-4) {$(-3,-4)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

